# This file is INERT — do not add exclusions here expecting them to apply.
#
# Docker reads `.dockerignore` from the build *context* root, and the
# backend image builds with the repo root as its context (it needs
# ingestion/ alongside backend/ — see the header of backend/Dockerfile).
# So the file that actually trims this image's context is /.dockerignore,
# not this one. The patterns that used to live here are all present there.
#
# Kept as a signpost rather than deleted, because an exclusion added here
# would silently do nothing — including one meant to keep a secret out of
# an image layer. Put it in /.dockerignore instead.
